  "boundary_sweep_note": "The frozen bundles all sit far from the threshold (negatives G/se~0, positive ~665), so agreement there tests the functional form but not the threshold VALUE. The sweep shrinks a real frozen dataset's interaction continuously across the boundary and checks the spec predicts the certificate's exact flip point -- where it can lose.",
  "interpretation": "The gap must exceed ~5 standard errors AND the measured route cost. Because se = sigma/sqrt(n), a workload with a small effect can only be certified by paying n >= (kappa*sigma/(G-c_route))^2 -- which is why the real workloads are unreachable, not merely unlucky.",
  "prohibited_extrapolations": [
    "any architecture claim",
    "L7",
    "L8",
    "kappa as a universal constant (it is design-specific)",
    "passing the screen implies routability (it only fails to exclude)"
  ]
}
